# Change-control manifest

agent-skills treats the agent as a **change-control system**, not only a coding assistant.

## Execution sequence (do not skip)

1. Observe
2. Reproduce (or prove not reproducible)
3. Isolate
4. Diagnose with evidence
5. Disprove alternatives
6. Assess impact and risk
7. Propose minimal patch
8. Verify
9. **Vault autolog** — mandatory after verified patch: [`vault-autolog.mdc`](workflow/vault-autolog.mdc) · reply `Vault daily: updated ...` or skip reason
10. Regression check — if the patch **redirected callers**, grep old symbols and remove zero-ref orphans per [`patching/callee-redirect-cleanup.mdc`](patching/callee-redirect-cleanup.mdc) before claiming done

**Never patch before diagnosis for unknown behavior.** Debug steps 1–4 or `/debug` when attached · known copy/UI → observe → patch · no mantra.

| Work type | Route |
|-----------|-------|
| Known copy/UI (outcome clear) | patch → verify → autolog — no `/debug` |
| Unknown bug / flaky / API fail | debug discipline; `/debug` optional |
| Unsure | One question: bug vs copy? |

## Patch budget (default)

| Limit | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Max files | 5 |
| Max lines changed (add+del) | 120 |

If exceeded: justify or split · `[BUDGET-OVERRIDE]` only with user approval.

## Confidence

| Confidence | Action |
|------------|--------|
| ≥ 0.9 + LOW risk | May patch |
| 0.7–0.89 | Propose; prefer review |
| < 0.7 | Diagnose only |

Stop if behavior unknown or multiple root causes plausible.

## Skill routing

Primary: [`decision-tree.mdc`](workflow/decision-tree.mdc). Skills apply when row matches — slash optional except full rituals (`/debug` mantra).

| Situation | Skill |
|-----------|--------|
| Unknown / stack trace | `/debug` |
| UI / mock / Figma SVG | `/builder-ui` |
| Cross-layer feature | `/builder-feature` (plan-only) |
| Review PR/plan | `/scrutinize` |
| Schema | `/builder-schema` |
| Git publish | `/git-push` |
| Pack meta | `/upgrade-ai` |
| RCA | `/fix-record` |

## Active skill precedence

When the user attaches or clearly invokes a skill whose **iron law** conflicts with the execution sequence above:

| Skill mode | Overrides |
|------------|-----------|
| `/builder-feature` (plan-only) | Steps 7–8 — **no application source patches**; hand off to builder-* per slice |
| `/scrutinize` (review-only) | **No patch** until review complete; recommend only until user approves changes |
| `/upgrade-ai` on pack | Meta edits only; app sequence N/A |

Iron law overrides steps 7–8 when active (`plan-only`, `review-only`).

## Production prohibitions

Speculative fixes · broad refactors in bugfixes · silent behavior changes · implicit API/schema breaks · unrelated rewrites.

## Rule layers

Always-on: this manifest + [`decision-tree`](workflow/decision-tree.mdc) + [`vault-autolog`](workflow/vault-autolog.mdc). Scoped: `ai-rules/{core,patching,architecture,testing,risk,workflow}/` (app source globs). Deep workflow: `ai-skills/*/reference.md`. Meta edits: [`/upgrade-ai`](../ai-skills/upgrade-ai/SKILL.md).
